# Phase 1 additions
.task-complete
# Phase 2 implementation-complete sentinel (L4): written into the working tree
# only after report + green gate + clean tree + honest verdict. Like
# .task-complete it is a gitignored working-tree marker, never committed, so the
# verify:all clean-tree assertion stays honest.
.phase-02-implementation-complete
# Acceptance marker: written into the working tree AFTER review passes and binds
# the reviewed HEAD (reviewed_head). Committing it would move HEAD and invalidate
# its own binding, so it is a gitignored working-tree artifact (like .task-complete),
# verified by scripts/check-acceptance.sh. Keeping it untracked also keeps the
# verify:all clean-tree assertion honest.
artifacts/phase-01/acceptance.json
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tmp
# Raw evidence must never enter git; only sanitized manifests are committed.
artifacts/phase-01/raw/
# Gate evidence bundle (P1-FINAL-CRIT-001). This is REGENERATED at the reviewed
# HEAD by scripts/capture-evidence.sh and its env-digest.txt records head_sha.
# If any of these files were tracked, writing them would move HEAD, so the
# recorded head_sha could never equal the commit that contains them — the exact
# staleness bug CRIT-001 flagged (evidence captured at caa1bff backing a marker
# for a later HEAD). Keeping the bundle untracked is what lets check-acceptance
# enforce env-digest.head_sha == reviewed_head == current HEAD.
artifacts/phase-01/env-digest.txt
artifacts/phase-01/env-digest.sha256
artifacts/phase-01/index.tsv
artifacts/phase-01/index.sha256
artifacts/phase-01/gates/
